# Allocation desk
#
# Shows:   the market side allocating what it filled — `allocate` from a `run`
#          block, `accepted`, `received`, `incomplete` and `rejected` on the
#          Ack, `replace allocation` after a refusal, `cancel allocation`,
#          `on sent allocation`
# Needs:   any active session; run it on LOOP-MKT with allocation-check
#          running on LOOP-CLI to be answered
# Watch:   Sent Allocations (Market menu): Status, Alloc Status and Rej Reason
#          as the Acks land; Received Allocations on the client side
# Outcome: an allocation of 500 across two accounts goes out and is accepted;
#          a second, wrongly totalled, is refused and then replaced with a
#          correct one, which is accepted; an allocation sent by hand and
#          still unanswered after a minute is cancelled

on error continue

run
    allocate symbol: 'IBM', side: buy, qty: 500, avg_price: 20.5, accounts: 'ACC1 300; ACC2 200',
    expect accepted or received or incomplete or rejected within 5s else fail 'no Ack'
    if event.kind == 'received'
        # Received is not yet accepted: the Ack that decides follows.
        expect accepted or rejected within 5s
    pass 'allocation ${allocation.alloc_id} is ${allocation.status}'

run
    # The accounts do not add up to the block: a careful counterparty refuses it.
    allocate symbol: 'IBM', side: buy, qty: 500, avg_price: 20.5, accounts: 'ACC1 300; ACC2 100',
    expect accepted or rejected within 5s
    if event.kind == 'rejected'
        log 'refused: ${allocation.alloc_rej_reason} — ${allocation.text}'
        # Terms left out keep the allocation's values; the row moves to the
        # new AllocID when the Ack accepts it.
        replace allocation accounts: 'ACC1 300; ACC2 200'
        expect accepted within 5s else fail 'the corrected allocation was refused too'
    pass 'settled as ${allocation.allocs}'

# An allocation sent from the Sent Allocations blotter by hand.
on sent allocation
    wait acked or timeout 1m
    if allocation.status == 'Sent'
        cancel allocation text: 'no answer'
